{"availability":"available","full":"CruxGarden/plasma-ui","name":"plasma-ui","description":"Liquid glass panels for React","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":273,"forks":26,"created":"2026-09-17T00:28:18Z","updated":"2026-10-07T02:17:41Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cruxgarden.github.io/plasma-ui/","topics":["animation","glassmorphism","liquid-glass","metaballs","mit-license","react","react-components","shaders","ui-components","webgl"],"demo":"https://cruxgarden.github.io/plasma-ui/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:16.014Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:16.014Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:16.014Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:16.014Z","stars":273,"forks":26}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Liquid components for React, rendered in WebGL on canvas, inspired by Apple's Liquid Glass design. The panel looks and behaves like liquid, with surface tension that fuses on contact with other panels. Anything visible behind the panel is refracted. And for layout convenience, the panels ultimately snap to a grid layout. The library is a work in progress, extracted from the Crux Garden project, but it seemed useful enough to share in its current form.","Status: 0.3.0. Core is stable and tested, but the API may change.","Zero dependencies, except for React. Best on desktop: the effect is GPU-heavy and does not run well on mobile."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/CruxGarden/plasma-ui/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"80603b12c2ed3ebc117f0cb9ffa4b8158c1def25340f4cd3e49668c67c4e43b8","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:16.172Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:16.172Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Liquid components for React, rendered in WebGL on canvas, inspired by Apple's Liquid Glass design. The panel looks and behaves like liquid, with surface tension that fuses on contact with other panels. Any